{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted → 0.725 acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality actually contributes meaningful signal beyond the RNA data. Config_019 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) is the cleanest single-variable ablation of config_001: it keeps the same RNA encoder (scvi_n200), same profile setting (multiprofile), and same aggregation (transformer), removing only the image branch and fusion. If config_019 matches or exceeds 0.725, the image modality is not adding value and the remaining 7 experiments should focus on RNA-encoder and aggregation choices within the RNA-only space. If config_001 is clearly superior, we confirm multimodal is the right direction and can then exploit by varying image encoder, fusion, or aggregation in subsequent experiments. This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most fundamental architectural decision with 8 experiments still in budget."
}

